course: dictionary
lesson: 14306
title: The word nutritional
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nutritional is about nutrition, which is the food a body needs to grow, have energy and stay healthy. «Children have different nutritional needs from adults.» Here nutritional tells you the needs are about food and health.
explain: Nutritional value is about how much good a food gives the body. «Carrots have a high nutritional value.» So carrots give your body a lot of good things, such as vitamins. Look at the words around nutritional to find its meaning: food, health, body and value are all clues.
explain: On food packets you will often see a «nutritional label». It shows the energy, fat, sugar, salt, protein and fibre in the food. Read it like a clue. The numbers tell you what the food gives your body, so you can compare two packets and choose the better one.
fact: Nutrition means the food a body needs to grow, have energy and stay healthy.
fact: «Nutritional» means to do with nutrition.
fact: «Nutritional value» means how much good a food gives the body.
fact: A «nutritional label» on a packet shows energy, fat, sugar, salt, protein and fibre, usually per 100 g or per serving.
fact: «Nutritionally» is the adverb: «The lunch was nutritionally balanced.» means the lunch gave the body a good mix of what it needs.
exercise: «Carrots have a high nutritional value.» What does nutritional value mean? | How the food tastes | How much a food costs in the shop | *How much good a food gives the body | How long a food stays fresh
exercise: Ella reads the «nutritional label» on a cereal box. What is she looking for? | The price of the box | A picture of a bowl | *The energy, fat, sugar and salt in the cereal | The name of the factory
exercise: Find and copy the word that means to do with the food a body needs. | packet | colour | *nutritional | cereal
test: «Growing children have different nutritional needs.» What does nutritional needs mean here? | The toys children like to play with | The places children visit on holiday | The clothes children wear to school | *The food a body needs to grow and stay healthy
test: «The school lunch was nutritionally balanced.» Which word is the adverb in this sentence? | *nutritionally | balanced | school | lunch
exam: Which sentence uses nutritional correctly? | «The nutritional bus took us to school.» | «She nutritional a fast run in the park.» | «The nutritional sky was bright and blue.» | *«The nutritional information on the packet shows how much sugar is in it.»
